good in combat situations too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T06:54:31-08:00","id":1469830,"title":"","content":"Even outside combat taking agency out of the target's hands is a good idea. You can use the increased Frenzy difficulty to induce behavior that is strategically bad for the situation, whatever this situations comes to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T08:56:24-08:00","id":1469842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469801-rego-vitae-question-dark-ages-vampire?p=1469811#post1469811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are three primary uses:<br /> 1. You can use this power on your allies to bypass generation limits and heal/buff them off-turn. It's a dif 5 roll, so you may reliably get 4-5 blood points spent where normally they'd only spend 1.<br /> 2. You can use this power on the enemies to waste their blood. Yes, it's technically not waste because it's put into attributes, but remember that blood buff past the generation limit +1 only lasts for one turn. And again - you can use 4-5 BPs like that. That's half to a quarter of their total blood supply gone. Good luck healing and using fancy blood magics now.<br /> 3. You can use it stealthily in social settings to provoke someone into rage. A tap on the shoulder and bam - dif 10 fear frenzy check from seeing a torch, dif 10 fury frenzy check from being called a dickwad. Though the torch one is good in combat situations too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! This is not clear from reading the rules in the book. It uses the words against their will, suggesting that it cannot be used on allies.<br /> <br /> The increase in stats would last for the entire scene or would they last for one turn only?<br /> <br /> Thanks again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T09:44:17-08:00","id":1469850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucardtes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469801-rego-vitae-question-dark-ages-vampire?p=1469842#post1469842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! This is not clear from reading the rules in the book. It uses the words against their will, suggesting that it cannot be used on allies.<br /> <br /> The increase in stats would last for the entire scene or would they last for one turn only?<br /> <br /> Thanks again.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use absolutely anything on your allies against their will. <hr />See the last sentence.<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/hkTVUhb.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T10:13:02-08:00","id":1469852,"title":"","content":"I worded my follow up poorly. If they are allowing the Tremere to use this power then it\u2019s not against their will. The description in the book doesn\u2019t mention that it can be used on allies (though it makes sense that it can).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T13:04:38-08:00","id":1469864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucardtes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469801-rego-vitae-question-dark-ages-vampire?p=1469852#post1469852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I worded my follow up poorly. If they are allowing the Tremere to use this power then it\u2019s not against their will. The description in the book doesn\u2019t mention that it can be used on allies (though it makes sense that it can).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule of thumb the rules don't distinguish allies and enemies. A target is a target and the rules tell you what happens to the target. In this context, <i>enemies</i> and, to a lesser degree, <i>against their will</i> are just fluff.<br /> <br /> Otherwise an enemy would be able to block your power simply by &quot;allowing&quot; it, so it ceases to be against their will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}